1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,040
The first thing you need to do is get clear on your intentions what is it that you want to do achieve accomplish learn in these 90 days.
首先明确自己的意图：这90天里，你想做什么、实现什么、学会什么？

2
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:17,040
Get really clear on it and make a very concrete goal maybe for example your goal is to really lack into school be super focused on studying on getting good grades.
明确一个具体目标，比如专注学业、认真学习、取得好成绩。

3
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:20,190
Maybe you want to get into a certain school or pass a certain test.
也许你想进入某所学校，或通过某个考试。

4
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:26,280
Maybe you want to start content creation and your goal in the next 90 days is like I want to get on my way to becoming a full time content creator.
也许你想开始创作内容，希望在90天里走上成为全职创作者的道路。

5
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:32,479
Maybe your goal is like physical fitness oriented and you're like you know I want to tone up I want to gain some muscle.
也许你的目标与体能有关，你想让身体更紧实、增加肌肉。

6
00:00:32,479 --> 00:00:34,880
I want to really get on my fitness grind in the next 90 days.
你想在接下来90天里认真投入健身。

7
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:46,119
The thing is if you're too general and too vague about this and you just say I want to eat healthier and drink more water and study more work harder work out stretch.
但如果目标太笼统、太模糊，只说想吃得健康、多喝水、多学习、努力工作、锻炼和拉伸……

8
00:00:46,119 --> 00:00:49,560
It's too much and you're not going to be able to really focus on one thing.
事情就太多了，你很难真正集中做一件事。

9
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:55,399
It's not that you can't do all of those things because you totally can but if you're starting from square one right now and you kind of.
不是说你不能做这些，你当然可以；但如果现在是从零开始……

10
00:00:55,399 --> 00:00:59,200
Don't really have a routine you're not really doing all of the healthy habits you want to do.
你还没有固定流程，也没有做到自己想培养的那些习惯。

11
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:04,120
And you try to just plunge yourself into doing every single routine in this really rigid schedule.
却试图一下投入每一个流程，排出非常僵硬的日程。

12
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:07,200
It's going to be really hard to actually keep up with this routine.
这样其实很难坚持这个流程。

13
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:11,319
What you really need to do is prioritize what is the most important to you in these 90 days.
你真正要做的是确定优先次序：这90天里什么对你最重要？

14
00:01:11,319 --> 00:01:14,910
One example for me is last year I really wanted to start a youtube channel.
比如去年，我非常想开一个 YouTube 频道。

15
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:19,760
I wanted to have accounts on other social media as well and grow those but I really wanted to be a youtuber.
我也想运营和发展其他社交平台的账号，但最想成为视频创作者。

16
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:25,239
I wanted to prioritize youtube as my main platform so I put in the work on youtube specifically.
我把 YouTube 作为主要平台，专门在这上面投入精力。

17
00:01:25,239 --> 00:01:31,080
I posted occasionally on those other platforms and I still am active on those other platforms but I made youtube be the priority.
我偶尔在其他平台发内容，也仍然活跃，但把 YouTube 放在首位。

18
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:35,680
I poured so much into youtube that the fruits of my labor were just snowballing.
我在 YouTube 投入很多，自己努力的成果也不断积累扩大。

19
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:39,910
Because I was putting so much time and effort and energy into it how could it not succeed.
我投入了那么多时间、努力和精力，她觉得这样怎么会不成功呢。

20
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:44,959
And I think it's okay to have a few goals stay really focused on these because it is 90 days that we're working with here.
我觉得可以有几个目标，但要专注，因为我们说的是90天。

21
00:01:44,959 --> 00:01:49,080
Which is a long time to make big progress but it's not like you can be super unrealistic ic.
90天可以取得很大进步，但也不能特别不切实际。

22
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:52,760
And be like okay well I've slacked off on my new year's resolutions all the way up until now.
不能说今年的新年计划一直拖到现在……

23
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:55,360
But now I'm going to do every single one it just might not be possible.
现在却打算把每一项都完成，那可能做不到。

24
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:59,159
So get clear on it and make sure that they are reasonable and doable goals.
所以要想清楚，确保这些目标合理、做得到。

25
00:01:59,159 --> 00:02:03,239
Next up establish a routine now that you have your goals and you know what you want to do.
接下来，建立流程。现在你已有目标，也知道自己想做什么。

26
00:02:03,239 --> 00:02:06,440
You have to figure out how these goals can fit into your daily life.
要想清楚这些目标如何融入你的日常生活。

27
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:14,440
If physical fitness is your goal if you want to lose some weight like burn some fat gain some muscle and spend some more time working out overall.
如果目标是体能，比如减重、减少脂肪、增加肌肉，或整体多运动一些……

28
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:17,799
You need to figure out where in your daily routine you can fit in a workout.
你需要找到日常流程中可以安排锻炼的时段。

29
00:02:17,799 --> 00:02:22,239
When you actually take the time to figure out how you're going to make your goal work how you're going to bring it to life.
当你真正花时间想清楚，如何让目标实现、落到实处……

30
00:02:22,239 --> 00:02:25,640
It makes it so much easier to implement those changes into your daily routine.
就更容易把这些改变落实到日常流程里。

31
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:31,680
I honestly recommend making a physical copy of your morning and night routine like literally write it down step by step.
我真心建议把早晚流程写下来，一步一步写清楚。

32
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:36,319
What are you going to do write in every healthy habit that you want to do in there again make sure that it's doable.
你要做什么？把想做的每个习惯写进去，再次确保可执行。

33
00:02:36,319 --> 00:02:40,200
The other really important thing with routines is actually scheduling in breaks for yourself.
流程中另一件重要的事，是给自己安排休息。

34
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:43,360
If you don't take breaks you are going to get burnt out really quickly.
如果不休息，你很快会感到精疲力竭。

35
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:49,439
And it's not reasonable to expect that you work non stop with no breaks because nobody can be their best selves with they do that.
期望自己不停工作、不休息并不合理，她认为这样没人能保持最佳状态。

36
00:02:49,439 --> 00:02:56,429
When I was in college last year I found that it was so so beneficial for me to actually take really small breaks between studying.
去年上大学时，我发现学习之间短暂休息对我很有帮助。

37
00:02:56,439 --> 00:03:01,360
Like maybe literally work for 30 minutes or do one assignment and then take like a 5 minute break.
比如学习30分钟，或做完一个作业，再休息约5分钟。

38
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:05,160
And go switch a load of laundry or go grab a snack or go make a cup of tea.
去换一批洗衣物、拿点零食，或泡杯茶。

39
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:09,120
And then after the 5 minutes come back because I would feel so refreshed from doing that.
5分钟后回来，我会觉得又有精神了。

40
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:14,680
I never felt burnt out and even if I had like a whole night's worth of homework to do and I really had a lot to do.
我没有觉得耗尽精力，即使有一整晚的作业、事情很多也是如此。

41
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:21,500
Just taking little breaks like that after I completed an assignment or worked for an hour hour or two it kept me fresh it kept my mind sharp.
做完作业或工作一两个小时后这样小憩，让我保持精神、头脑清醒。
